From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:30:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0218: the display blends a layer over another

An app drawing with Metal (MetalHello, CAMetalLayer) showed in horizontal
bands of black that moved between boots, though its drawable and IOSurface
read back whole. backboardd hands the app's full-screen layer to the
display as layer 0 and its own buffer (status bar, transparent elsewhere)
as layer 1. present() copied each layer raw: layer 0 on the CPU (17 ms,
not the size the GPU blit takes), then layer 1 with the GPU blit, not
waited for, over the whole panel. Layers over another are now blended
(premultiplied BGRA, source over) on the CPU, into a cacheable shadow of
the panel copied out once (reading the panel itself took 1.1 s a frame).
---
diff -ru a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp	2026-11-25 13:00:13
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp	2026-11-25 13:23:50
@@ -34,6 +34,29 @@
  */
 #include "SweetSurface.h"
 
+/*
+ * 0218: a layer over another is blended, not copied: premultiplied BGRA, source over. backboardd hands an app's
+ * full-screen CAMetalLayer to the display as layer 0 and its own mostly transparent buffer (status bar) as layer 1;
+ * copied raw, layer 1's clear pixels showed as black bands over the app.
+ */
+static inline uint32_t
+sweet_fb_over(uint32_t s, uint32_t d)
+{
+	uint32_t a = s >> 24;
+	if (a == 0xff) {
+		return s;
+	}
+	if (a == 0) {
+		return d;
+	}
+	uint32_t k = 255 - a;
+	uint32_t rb = (d & 0x00ff00ffu) * k + 0x00800080u;
+	rb = ((rb + ((rb >> 8) & 0x00ff00ffu)) >> 8) & 0x00ff00ffu;
+	uint32_t ag = ((d >> 8) & 0x00ff00ffu) * k + 0x00800080u;
+	ag = (ag + ((ag >> 8) & 0x00ff00ffu)) & 0xff00ff00u;
+	return s + rb + ag;
+}
+
